# Rembric server configuration.
#
# Copy this file to `.env`, fill in the required values, and run:
#     docker compose up -d
#
# `.env` is gitignored; never commit your secrets.

# ── Required ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Generate once and keep it secret:  openssl rand -hex 32
REMBRIC_ADMIN_TOKEN=

# ── Image version pin ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Default unset = `:latest`. Pin to a specific tag for reproducible
# deploys (recommended once a version proves stable in your setup):
# REMBRIC_VERSION=0.13.0

# ── Common toggles (uncomment to override defaults) ────────────────
# REMBRIC_PORT=8787
# LOG_LEVEL=info

# ── Container resource caps (uncomment to override defaults) ───────
# Both default to 0 = unlimited, i.e. the host decides — the same
# behaviour as before these knobs existed. Set them if rembric shares a
# machine with workloads you care about more.
#
# CPU ceiling. Docker REFUSES TO START the container if this exceeds the
# cores the host actually has, so leave it at 0 unless you know the
# number. The embedder pins its own thread pool to at most 2 cores, so
# values above ~2 buy little:
# REMBRIC_CPUS=2
#
# Memory ceiling. Exceeding it gets the process OOM-killed, so do not set
# it tight: the ONNX embedding model alone is ~800 MiB resident, and the
# server plus SQLite page cache sit on top. Below ~1.5g is asking for a
# crash loop:
# REMBRIC_MEMORY=2g
#
# Task (process + thread) ceiling. Defaults to 512, which is ~20x what a
# healthy instance uses; it exists to contain a runaway thread leak:
# REMBRIC_PIDS_LIMIT=512

# ── Advanced knobs (uncomment to override defaults) ────────────────
# Rate limiting (off by default; enable for multi-agent deployments):
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false
# RATE_LIMIT_RPS=10
# RATE_LIMIT_BURST=30

# Sessions sweep: how old an 'active' session can be at startup before
# it's flipped to 'abandoned'. Default 24h. Floor 60s, ceiling 30 days:
# SESSION_ABANDON_AFTER_MS=86400000

# Save-time candidate detection (fresh-context judgment):
# CANDIDATES_PER_SAVE_MAX=5
# CANDIDATE_VEC_THRESHOLD=0.85
# CANDIDATE_FTS_THRESHOLD=0.4

# Pending judgments older than this surface in memory.context for the
# agent to close with memory.judge. Default 24h:
# JUDGMENT_ORPHAN_AFTER_MS=86400000

# Pending judgments no agent closed within this window are orphaned by
# the deterministic sweep. Default 14 days:
# JUDGMENT_ORPHAN_DEADLINE_MS=1209600000

# Data-loss guard bypass: set to "1" ONLY when intentionally restoring a
# backup/snapshot that drops a monitored table (memory, projects, sessions,
# tokens, prompts) to under half the count the server last saw — the guard
# refuses to boot on that, since it is indistinguishable from an accidental
# overwrite. It must be set HERE and not in your shell: the compose service
# only passes this file through env_file. Comment it out again after the
# restore boots successfully — it is a one-time acknowledgment, not a
# standing config flag. See docs/backup.md#restoring-a-snapshot.
# REMBRIC_ALLOW_DATA_SHRINKAGE=1

# Full reference: README.md#configuration  +  src/config.ts
